-- THE JOIN and THE DEADLINE as values in a join line's WITHIN (refusal 3 of
-- §5.1.1.1, ratified for the value by §2.6 card B1): that WITHIN is the
-- group's deadline, so it is what THE DEADLINE would name, and the group's
-- join has not fired when it is read. Refused in the duration and in the
-- anchor alike, even nested under an obligation that has both.

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Tenant HAS name IS A STRING

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    Sign HAS signer IS AN Actor
    Pay  HAS amount IS A NUMBER

alice MEANS Tenant OF "Alice"

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`in the anchor` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t MUST Sign t ONCE ALL HAVE WITHIN 0 OF (THE JOIN PLUS 14) HENCE FULFILLED

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`in the duration, nested` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign alice WITHIN 10
    HENCE (EVERY Tenant t MUST Sign t ONCE ALL HAVE WITHIN THE DEADLINE MINUS 3 HENCE FULFILLED)
